{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>All in whose nostrils was the breath of the spirit of life.</b> From here it is clear that the soul departs through the nose at a person's death, and from there it also enters, as it is written (Genesis 2:7): ״ויפח באפיו נשמת חיים״ — and there I expounded at length in its place." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: כל אשר נשמת רוח חיים באפיו — the word כל alludes to the quality of כל אשר בה, by means of which Avraham our father, peace be upon him, was blessed, and this is the tenth sefirah, and from there the souls fly forth. And this is why our Rabbis, of blessed memory, enacted the recitation on the Sabbath day of נשמת כל חי — 'the soul of all that lives' — for in it He rested and was refreshed (וינפש), and it is the wellspring of blessings and the foundation of life; and this is the meaning of ״ויברך אלהים את יום השביעי״. Therefore it says אשר נשמת רוח חיים באפיו, thereby including all mankind, in whom there is נשמת חיים — the breath of life — while the other possessors of the soul of movement also have within them רוח חיים — a spirit of life — but not נשמת חיים. And by this He made known the totality of all living beings, and alluded to the quality (midah) that is the cause of the life of all that lives. And there is a great matter to be roused to ask regarding its reason, for it appears as one great outpouring, with nothing else like it in Scripture; and understand this." "<b>Of all that was on the dry land, died</b> — and not the fish of the sea. The fish were saved because they fled to Oceanus, and the flood was not upon the sea but only upon the earth, as it is written: ״ויהי הגשם על הארץ״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:07.092688986Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}